\", \"value\": 2.5}, ...]}\n\nDo I include \"unit_id\": null at attribute level? The example shows only unit_symbol at attribute level. Follow example.\n\nconfig_level:\n{\"attribute\": \"mpe_upper_flowrate_zone\", \"axis\": \"water_temperature\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"water temperature > 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -3, \"max\": 3}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n]}\n\n{\"attribute\": \"q1\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"axis\": \"model × q3/q1 ratio\", \"values\": [20 entries]}\n{\"attribute\": \"q2\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"axis\": \"model × q3/q1 ratio\", \"values\": [20 entries]}\n\nCondition strings: \"UL 2.5 (DN 15/20), Q3/Q1 = 800\" etc.\n\nLet me write all q1/q2 conditions:\n1. \"UL 2.5 (DN 15/20), Q3/Q1 = 800\": q1 0.003, q2 0.005\n2. \"UL 2.5 (DN 15/20), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.006, q2 0.010\n3. \"UL 2.5 (DN 15/20), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.010, q2 0.016\n4. \"UL 4 (DN 20), Q3/Q1 = 800\": q1 0.005, q2 0.008\n5. \"UL 4 (DN 20), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.010, q2 0.016\n6. \"UL 4 (DN 20), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.016, q2 0.026\n7. \"UL 6.3 (DN 25), Q3/Q1 = 800\": q1 0.008, q2 0.013\n8. \"UL 6.3 (DN 25), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.016, q2 0.025\n9. \"UL 6.3 (DN 25), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.025, q2 0.040\n10. \"UL 10 (DN 25/32), Q3/Q1 = 800\": q1 0.013, q2 0.020\n11. \"UL 10 (DN 25/32), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.025, q2 0.040\n12. \"UL 10 (DN 25/32), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.040, q2 0.064\n13. \"UL 16 (Q3=10), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.025, q2 0.040\n14. \"UL 16 (Q3=10), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.040, q2 0.064\n15. \"UL 16 (Q3=16), Q3/Q1 = 800\": q1 0.020, q2 0.032\n16. \"UL 16 (Q3=16), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.040, q2 0.064\n17. \"UL 16 (Q3=16), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.064, q2 0.102\n18. \"UL 25 (DN 50), Q3/Q1 = 500\": q1 0.050, q2 0.080\n19. \"UL 25 (DN 50), Q3/Q1 = 400\": q1 0.0625, q2 0.100\n20. \"UL 25 (DN 50), Q3/Q1 = 250\": q1 0.100, q2 0.160\n\nModel-level q3: UL2.5: 2.50, UL4: 4.00, UL6.3: 6.30, UL10: 10.00, UL16(Q3=10): 10.00, UL16(Q3=16): 16.00, UL25: 25.0.\nq4: 3.13, 5.00, 7.88, 12.50, 12.50, 20.00, 31.3.\n\nNote UL25 q4=31.3 (25×1.25=31.25, rounded 31.3). ✓.\n\nconnection_type per model:\n- UL 2.5: \"G ¾ B or G ⅞ B / G ¾ B or G 1 B\" — hmm. Should I clarify? The two DN options. I'll write \"G ¾ B or G ⅞ B (DN 15); G ¾ B or G 1 B (DN 20)\". Risk of over-interpretation. The \"/\" in raw separates the two DN columns' contents. I think adding the DN annotations is a faithful and helpful interpretation. But \"don't fabricate\"... it's an inference. I'll keep the raw: \"G ¾ B or G ⅞ B / G ¾ B or G 1 B\". Meh. Let me keep raw string exactly.\n- UL 4: \"G 1 B\"\n- UL 6.3: \"G 1 ¼ B\"\n- UL 10: \"G 1 ¼ B or G 1 ½ B\"\n- UL 16: \"G 2 B or flange\"\n- UL 25: \"G 2 ½ B or flange\"\n\nlength_brass_body: {min,max} in mm: UL2.5 {80,165}, UL4 {105,190}, UL6.3 {105,190}, UL10 {165,260}, UL16(both) {260,300}, UL25 {200,300}.\n\nlength_composite_body: UL2.5 {80,110}, UL4 {105,130}, UL6.3 {105,130}, UL10 null, UL16s null, UL25 null.\n\nFor null values in model_level values: {\"model\": \"UL 10\", \"value\": null}. OK.\n\nAlternatively omit those models from length_composite values — but then it looks like missing data. null conveys \"not available\" better. Keep null.\n\nq3_over_q1 model_level: strings \"800; 400; 250\" etc.\n\npressure_loss_class: \"ΔP40\"/\"ΔP25\" strings.\n\nnominal_diameter_dn values: \"15 / 20\" (string) for UL2.5; 20; 25; \"25 / 32\"; 40; 40; 50.\n\nNow revision_history: [{\"revision\": \"0\", \"date\": \"2021-10-15\", \"changes\": \"Issuing certificate\"}]. Hmm the table says \"Addition 0\". Maybe revision: \"Addition 0\". The instruction: revision string e.g. \"0\" not 0. I'll use \"Addition 0\" — it's the literal label. Actually \"e.g. '0'\" suggests they want the numeric-ish string. \"Addition 0\" is the revision identifier here. I'll go with \"Addition 0\". Hmm... I'll do \"0\" with changes \"Issuing certificate\". Which is better? The cert calls it \"Addition 0\" (CMI's scheme for additions/revisions). I'll use \"Addition 0\".\n\nWait, also page 1 says the certificate number ends \"-2021.05\" and history shows Addition 0 issued 15 October 2021. OK.\n\nissuing_authority.website: not present. phone/email: not present. omit.\n\noiml_issuer_id: not present anywhere (no issuer ID number). omit.\n\nNow let me also double-check: \"For accuracy class (if applicable): 2\" — accuracy_classes: [2]. R49 classes are 1, 2, 3. ✓.\n\nEd.: R49 edition 2013 (R 49-1:2013 etc.). edition: 2013 (int).\n\nNow assemble the JSON. Watch JSON validity: no trailing commas, proper escaping. Unicode chars (¾, ⅞, ¼, ½, ³, Δ, ≤, ×) are fine in JSON.\n\nLet me also double check indicating range \"999 999\" → 999999 m³.\n\n\"Verze 20-001\" is a form version — not certificate revision; ignore.\n\nAlso note: scheme A — the \"A\" appears in cert number and title.\n\nLet me draft description for certified_type:\n\n\"Ultrasonic water meter designed to measure, memorise and display the volume at metering conditions of water passing through the measurement transducer. Consists of a brass or composite body with connecting screw threads, one pair of ultrasonic transducers and an electronic indicating device formed by an LCD display showing volume and flow. Two indication modes: normal resolution mode and high resolution mode (used during calibration) displaying volume resolution of 0.00001 m³. No buttons; adjustment and reading/setting of metrological data realised electronically using NFC, access secured by password. Legally non-relevant communication possible by radio module with frequency 433 MHz, 434 MHz or 868 MHz (radio module not part of this certificate). Separation of software; SW versions and CRCs displayed on LCD. Installation in arbitrary orientation; not designed to measure reverse flow. Sealed by embedding the clamp-on cover to the meter body; electronic tamper detection shown on LCD.\"\n\nGood.\n\nmatrix_tables descriptions: brief.\n\nNow, about \"components\": the certificate doesn't name sub-assemblies as separate certified modules — module designation \"-\". Omit components.\n\nfootnotes: none. Omit.\n\nLet me now write out the full JSON.\n\nAlso: \"V 3112\" logo — ignore.\n\nOne more check on test report 1: \"No. 0511-ER-V029-21 dated 7 October 2021 that includes 62 pages including annex 1\" — role type_evaluation_report (\"OIML type evaluation report\" referenced). ✓ pages: 62.\n\nDocumentation file: \"0511-UL-V029-21\" — role documentation_file, in test_reports array (schema puts it there).\n\nFinal JSON structure:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2021.05\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 6,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2021-10-15\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"APATOR POWOGAZ S.A.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"ul. Klemensa Janickiego 23/25\", \"60-542 Poznań\", \"Poland\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    { same }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"ULTRIMIS (UL)\", \"UL 2.5\", \"UL 4\", \"UL 6.3\", \"UL 10\", \"UL 16\", \"UL 25\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"Not applicable\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL)\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 2.5\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 2.5, DN 15/20\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 4\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 4, DN 20\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 6.3\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 6.3, DN 25\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 10\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 10, DN 25/32\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 16 (Q3=10)\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 16, DN 40, Q3=10 m³/h\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 16 (Q3=16)\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 16, DN 40, Q3=16 m³/h\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"UL 25\", \"label\": \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 25, DN 50\", \"attributes\": {}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {...},\n    \"model_level\": [...],\n    \"config_level\": [...]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [2]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [...]\n}\n\nWait: labels — \"ULTRIMIS (UL) 2.5\" hmm, the type is \"ULTRIMIS (UL)\" and models \"UL 2.5\". Label fine.\n\nNow type_level entries with full structured objects. Let me write them:\n\n\"q2_over_q1\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n\"q3_over_q4\": {\"value\": 1.25, ...}\n\"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"ultrasonic\", ...}\n\"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": 2, ...}\n\"mpe_lower_flowrate_zone\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -5, \"max\": 5}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\", ...}\n\"temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T30, T50\", ...}\n\"water_pressure_class\": {\"value\": \"MAP 10, MAP 16\", ...}\n\"environmental_class\": {\"value\": \"B or O\", ...}\n\"electromagnetic_environment_class\": {\"value\": \"E1, E2\", ...}\n\"maximum_admissible_temperature\": {\"value\": 50, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\", \"unit_id\": \"u:degree_Celsius\", ...}\n\"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\", ...}\n\"orientation_limitation\": {\"value\": \"any\", ...}\n\"indicating_range\": {\"value\": 999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\", ...}\n\"indicating_device_resolution\": {\"value\": 0.001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\", ...}\n\"rapid_test_device_resolution\": {\"value\": 0.00001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\", ...}\n\"eut_test_category\": {\"value\": \"Ultrasonic water meters\", ...}\n\"eut_test_case\": {\"value\": \"B\", ...}\n\"minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", ...}\n\"minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", ...}\n\"installation_sensitivity_class\": {\"value\": \"U0D0\", ...}\n\"flow_conditioner_required\": {\"value\": \"No\", ...}\n\"power_supply_type\": {\"value\": \"non-replaceable battery\", ...}\n\"u_max\": {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\", ...}\n\"u_min\": {\"value\": 1.9, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\", ...}\n\"minimum_battery_life_time\": {\"value\": 10, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\", ...}\n\"legally_relevant_software_version_crc\": {\"value\": \"03.00 / 5563; 04.01 / 235E; 04.10 / 62C7611F\", ...}\n\nmodel_level:\n1. {\"attribute\": \"nominal_diameter_dn\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\n   {\"model\": \"UL 2.5\", \"value\": \"15 / 20\"},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 4\", \"value\": 20},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 6.3\", \"value\": 25},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 10\", \"value\": \"25 / 32\"},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 16 (Q3=10)\", \"value\": 40},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 16 (Q3=16)\", \"value\": 40},\n   {\"model\": \"UL 25\", \"value\": 50}\n]}\n2. {\"attribute\": \"q3\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [\n   UL 2.5: 2.50, UL 4: 4.00, UL 6.3: 6.30, UL 10: 10.00, UL 16 (Q3=10): 10.00, UL 16 (Q3=16): 16.00, UL 25: 25.0\n]}\n3. {\"attribute\": \"q4\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [3.13, 5.00, 7.88, 12.50, 12.50, 20.00, 31.3]}\n4. {\"attribute\": \"q3_over_q1\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\"800; 400; 250\" ×4..., \"400; 250\", \"800; 400; 250\", \"500; 400; 250\"]}\n5. {\"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\"ΔP40\" ×6, \"ΔP25\"]}\n6. {\"attribute\": \"connection_type_screw_thread\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [...strings]}\n7. {\"attribute\": \"length_brass_body\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", \"values\": [ranges]}\n8. {\"attribute\": \"length_composite_body\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", \"values\": [{80,110},{105,130},{105,130},null,null,null,null]}\n\nHmm — model_level values with unit at attribute level and value plain: consistent with R137 example. But rule 2's strict shape... The R137 example is authoritative for model_level. For ranges in model_level values: value as {\"min\":80,\"max\":165}. OK.\n\nActually hmm, for consistency and per rule 2 \"Every characteristic value MUST be an object with this shape\" — there's tension. The examples show model_level values as plain {model, value}. I'll go with the examples. For type_level I use the full shape.\n\nShould model_level values include footnote_markers? None needed.\n\nconfig_level:\n\n1. mpe_upper_flowrate_zone:\n{\"attribute\": \"mpe_upper_flowrate_zone\", \"axis\": \"water_temperature\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"water temperature > 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -3, \"max\": 3}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n]}\n2. q1 (20 entries), axis: \"model_and_q3_q1_ratio\"\n3. q2 (20 entries), same axis.\n\nmatrix_tables (5 entries):\n\n1. {\n  \"name\": \"Flowrates — models UL 2.5 and UL 4\",\n  \"columns\": [\"model_number\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\", \"q3_over_q1\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 2.5\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": \"15 / 20\", \"q3_over_q1\": 800, \"q1\": 0.003, \"q2\": 0.005, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q4\": 3.13},\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 2.5\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": \"15 / 20\", \"q3_over_q1\": 400, \"q1\": 0.006, \"q2\": 0.010, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q4\": 3.13},\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 2.5\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": \"15 / 20\", \"q3_over_q1\": 250, \"q1\": 0.010, \"q2\": 0.016, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q4\": 3.13},\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 4\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": 20, \"q3_over_q1\": 800, \"q1\": 0.005, \"q2\": 0.008, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0},\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 4\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": 20, \"q3_over_q1\": 400, \"q1\": 0.010, \"q2\": 0.016, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0},\n    {\"model_number\": \"UL 4\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": 20, \"q3_over_q1\": 250, \"q1\": 0.016, \"q2\": 0.026, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q4\": 5.0}\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"...\",\n  \"footnotes\": []\n}\n\n2. Flowrates UL 6.3 and UL 10.\n3. Flowrates UL 16 (columns include q3 since it varies by row).\n4. Flowrates UL 25.\n5. Installation details by model.\n\nFor table 3 columns: [\"model_number\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\", \"q3\", \"q3_over_q1\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q4\"], units [null, null, \"m³/h\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\"].\n\nRows:\n{\"model_number\": \"UL 16\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": 40, \"q3\": 10.0, \"q3_over_q1\": 400, \"q1\": 0.025, \"q2\": 0.040, \"q4\": 12.5},\n{\"...\", \"q3\": 10.0, \"q3_over_q1\": 250, \"q1\": 0.040, \"q2\": 0.064, \"q4\": 12.5},\n{\"q3\": 16.0, \"q3_over_q1\": 800, \"q1\": 0.020, \"q2\": 0.032, \"q4\": 20.0},\n{\"q3\": 16.0, \"q3_over_q1\": 400, \"q1\": 0.040, \"q2\": 0.064, \"q4\": 20.0},\n{\"q3\": 16.0, \"q3_over_q1\": 250, \"q1\": 0.064, \"q2\": 0.102, \"q4\": 20.0}\n\nTable 4:\n{\"model_number\": \"UL 25\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": 50, \"q3_over_q1\": 500, \"q1\": 0.050, \"q2\": 0.080, \"q3\": 25.0, \"q4\": 31.3},\n{400, 0.0625, 0.100, 25.0, 31.3},\n{250, 0.100, 0.160, 25.0, 31.3}\n\nTable 5 installation:\ncolumns: [\"model_number\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\", \"connection_type_screw_thread\", \"length_brass_body\", \"length_composite_body\"], column_units [null, null, null, \"mm\", \"mm\"].\nrows:\n{\"model_number\": \"UL 2.5\", \"nominal_diameter_dn\": \"15 / 20\", \"connection_type_screw_thread\": \"G ¾ B or G ⅞ B / G ¾ B or G 1 B\", \"length_brass_body\": \"80 – 165\", \"length_composite_body\": \"80 - 110\"},\n{\"UL 4\", 20, \"G 1 B\", \"105-190\", \"105-130\"},\n{\"UL 6.3\", 25, \"G 1 ¼ B\", \"105 - 190\", \"105 - 130\"},\n{\"UL 10\", \"25 / 32\", \"G 1 ¼ B or G 1 ½ B\", \"165 - 260\", \"-\"},\n{\"UL 16\", 40, \"G 2 B or flange\", \"260; 300\", \"-\"},\n{\"UL 25\", 50, \"G 2 ½ B or flange\", \"200 - 300\", \"-\"}\ndescription: \"Source table 'Installation details'. For UL 16 the brass-body length appears as two separate cells ('260', '300') in the source, indicating available lengths 260 mm and 300 mm. '-' = not available.\"\nfootnotes: []\n\nOK. Also add matrix table for basic technical data? Skipping.\n\ntest_reports:\n[\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V029-21\", \"date\": \"2021-10-07\", \"pages\": 62, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P5006-21\", \"pages\": 91, \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P5007-21\", \"pages\": 53, \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6011-PT-SW024-21\", \"pages\": 3, \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"8551-PT-E0054-21\", \"pages\": 7, \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-UL-V029-21\", \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n]\n\nrevision_history:\n[{\"revision\": \"Addition 0\", \"date\": \"2021-10-15\", \"changes\": \"Issuing certificate\"}]\n\nDouble-check nothing else: \"Marking and inscriptions\" — descriptive; covered in description? Could add marking requirements summary but optional. Skip.\n\nCheck JSON: unicode ¾ (U+00BE), ⅞ (U+215E), ¼ (U+00BC), ½ (U+00BD), Δ, ³, ≤, ×, ř (Klenovský), ů, ż? \"Poznań\" has ń. Fine.\n\nDescription string must escape quotes — I'll avoid double quotes inside.\n\nLet me write the final JSON carefully.\n\nOne consideration: \"date_issued\" — \"15 October 2021\" → \"2021-10-15\". ✓\n\nAlso certificate.project_number omitted, oiml_issuer_id omitted.\n\nFinal check on the \"certificate.number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2021.05\". ✓\n\nWrite it out now.",
